(1376818, 174364, 23456, '<td valign="top">A bit too much black, it does detract and takes up the most part of the photo. This would look better in B/W IMO.</td>', 'A bit too much black, it does detract and takes up the most part of the photo. This would look better in B/W IMO.', '2005-05-11 01:01:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376832, 174313, 23456, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and a fitting title. Love the colour did you use duotone for this ? If anything I''d crop in slightly . Well done !</td>', 'Nice composition and a fitting title. Love the colour did you use duotone for this ? If anything I''d crop in slightly . Well done !', '2005-05-11 01:03:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376841, 174581, 23098, '<td valign="top">That would be scary!</td>', 'That would be scary!', '2005-05-11 01:05:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376858, 173276, 23098, '<td valign="top">Interesting -  great sky background.  Nice shot.</td>', 'Interesting -  great sky background.  Nice shot.', '2005-05-11 01:08:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376869, 173338, 23456, '<td valign="top">nice, maybe just a little too dark IMO</td>', 'nice, maybe just a little too dark IMO', '2005-05-11 01:09:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376873, 174066, 23098, '<td valign="top">I can feel the freedom - nice work!</td>', 'I can feel the freedom - nice work!', '2005-05-11 01:09:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376902, 173344, 23098, '<td valign="top">Good idea! Like it a lot.</td>', 'Good idea! Like it a lot.', '2005-05-11 01:13:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1376914, 173059, 23456, '<td valign="top">I love this effect and well composed !</td>', 'I love this effect and well composed !', '2005-05-11 01:15:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377327, 172135, 10261, '<td valign="top">I can''t decide whether the people in the foreground add to or detract from my enjoyment of this image. I think that a shallower DOF which made it clear whether the statues or the people looking at the statues were the intended subject of this picture would help to remove that dilemma.</td>', 'I can''t decide whether the people in the foreground add to or detract from my enjoyment of this image. I think that a shallower DOF which made it clear whether the statues or the people looking at the statues were the intended subject of this picture would help to remove that dilemma.', '2005-05-11 04:13:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377328, 172944, 25022, '<td valign="top">very calming composition and could benefit if the palm feathers were cloned out as they detract one''s attention from the boat and the sun.  This applies to the buoy behind the boat as well.  You could also have fixed the ''horizon'' where the hills meet the water as in seems to be slightly tilted.  Still a very suggestive snapshot.</td>', 'very calming composition and could benefit if the palm feathers were cloned out as they detract one''s attention from the boat and the sun.  This applies to the buoy behind the boat as well.  You could also have fixed the ''horizon'' where the hills meet the water as in seems to be slightly tilted.  Still a very suggestive snapshot.', '2005-05-11 04:14:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377332, 173987, 10261, '<td valign="top">You dream of _golf_? Why, that''s enough to put a guy to sleep.<br/> <br/>I think that this would have been a stronger shot (photographically) if the shadows from the trees weren''t so prominent. Conversely, if this were _my_ picture, the dream would be a nightmare, and I''d render this in sepia and crank the contrast to emphasize the shadows. The shadow from the tree at about 12 o''clock looks like it''s reaching down to grab the unsuspecting golfer.</td>', 'You dream of _golf_? Why, that''s enough to put a guy to sleep. I think that this would have been a stronger shot (photographically) if the shadows from the trees weren''t so prominent. Conversely, if this were _my_ picture, the dream would be a nightmare, and I''d render this in sepia and crank the contrast to emphasize the shadows. The shadow from the tree at about 12 o''clock looks like it''s reaching down to grab the unsuspecting golfer.', '2005-05-11 04:18:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377333, 174505, 25022, '<td valign="top">Wonderful drive-in but the person jars with the overall composition in wearing blue jeans and an orange t-shirt.  As is he''s a glaring disjunction to the harmony of the blooming trees and flowers.</td>', 'Wonderful drive-in but the person jars with the overall composition in wearing blue jeans and an orange t-shirt.  As is he''s a glaring disjunction to the harmony of the blooming trees and flowers.', '2005-05-11 04:22:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377336, 174584, 10261, '<td valign="top">Freud would certainly have fun with this one. On a strictly photographic note, the blurry leaf / wing-looking-thing in the background looks like it may be an intentional repetition of the form of the fly''s wings, or it may just be some blurry thing in the background. If it was intended, having it oriented in a cardinal position relative to the fly (e.g. offset 90, 180, 270, or 360 degrees from either of the fly''s wings) would have enhanced the effect. Posing the fly would, of course, be the hard part. If the repetition was unintentional (or the fly just wouldn''t pose), you may have been better off narrowing the DOF a bit further to reduce the clear lines in the background.</td>', 'Freud would certainly have fun with this one. On a strictly photographic note, the blurry leaf / wing-looking-thing in the background looks like it may be an intentional repetition of the form of the fly''s wings, or it may just be some blurry thing in the background. If it was intended, having it oriented in a cardinal position relative to the fly (e.g. offset 90, 180, 270, or 360 degrees from either of the fly''s wings) would have enhanced the effect. Posing the fly would, of course, be the hard part. If the repetition was unintentional (or the fly just wouldn''t pose), you may have been better off narrowing the DOF a bit further to reduce the clear lines in the background.', '2005-05-11 04:25:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377338, 174400, 10261, '<td valign="top">I like the effect, but since the focus of flow is directed at the end of the stone bridge, it would be nice to see something specific there to look at (e.g. someone leaning against the bridge''s railing).</td>', 'I like the effect, but since the focus of flow is directed at the end of the stone bridge, it would be nice to see something specific there to look at (e.g. someone leaning against the bridge''s railing).', '2005-05-11 04:27:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377342, 173923, 10261, '<td valign="top">The hint of purple / lilac in the bottom left corner draws my eyes out of the frame (which is presumably not your intent in this case). The grainy feel of the photo seems appropriate, but I think that a slightly softer focus may have enhanced the dreamy / nostalgic feel of the picture. Nice DOF.</td>', 'The hint of purple / lilac in the bottom left corner draws my eyes out of the frame (which is presumably not your intent in this case). The grainy feel of the photo seems appropriate, but I think that a slightly softer focus may have enhanced the dreamy / nostalgic feel of the picture. Nice DOF.', '2005-05-11 04:30:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377345, 173011, 10261, '<td valign="top">The way this is framed splits the image in half, seemingly the "white, cloudy sky" half and the "deep blue sky punctuated with fluffy clouds" side. If this split was intentional, I''d be more interested in seeing more of the blue side (e.g. to the end of the palm fronds) and less of the white. I really like the perspective, but I think that this may have been a more interesting composition if the tree split the frame at a more interesting angle (e.g. from the bottom left corner to the top right corner). Using a shallower DOF might have also offered some interesting alternatives.</td>', 'The way this is framed splits the image in half, seemingly the "white, cloudy sky" half and the "deep blue sky punctuated with fluffy clouds" side. If this split was intentional, I''d be more interested in seeing more of the blue side (e.g. to the end of the palm fronds) and less of the white. I really like the perspective, but I think that this may have been a more interesting composition if the tree split the frame at a more interesting angle (e.g. from the bottom left corner to the top right corner). Using a shallower DOF might have also offered some interesting alternatives.', '2005-05-11 04:36:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377346, 173823, 10261, '<td valign="top">This appears to be a partially open flower bud. In general, macro shots of flowers look better if the flower has been lightly misted with water. Something about the light and focus here strikes me as somewhat overly-homogeneous. I''d like to see either a bit more contrast from the light or a bit more texture in the petals; as it is, I see a yellowish/pinkish/reddish flower with very little texture or depth to it. The way your subject is framed lends a bit of ambiguity to the item depicted, but I think that the focus would need to be a bit softer for this to be sufficiently enigmatic.</td>', 'This appears to be a partially open flower bud. In general, macro shots of flowers look better if the flower has been lightly misted with water. Something about the light and focus here strikes me as somewhat overly-homogeneous. I''d like to see either a bit more contrast from the light or a bit more texture in the petals; as it is, I see a yellowish/pinkish/reddish flower with very little texture or depth to it. The way your subject is framed lends a bit of ambiguity to the item depicted, but I think that the focus would need to be a bit softer for this to be sufficiently enigmatic.', '2005-05-11 04:42:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377348, 173379, 10261, '<td valign="top">And it appears that you can do so in color. I think that the eyes would have been a stronger focal point if they had more detail or a more well-defined catchlight. The selective desaturation only draws my attention to the fact that I can''t even distinguish between her pupil and iris. Most of the detail on the face is blown out (which again draws attention to the eyes), but there are still a few well-defined, large freckles. Since advanced editing was allowed, you could have cloned these out, but I might have preferred it if you''d have left more of the detail in whichever channel contained the freckles, which would have preserved the contours of your model''s face.</td>', 'And it appears that you can do so in color. I think that the eyes would have been a stronger focal point if they had more detail or a more well-defined catchlight. The selective desaturation only draws my attention to the fact that I can''t even distinguish between her pupil and iris. Most of the detail on the face is blown out (which again draws attention to the eyes), but there are still a few well-defined, large freckles. Since advanced editing was allowed, you could have cloned these out, but I might have preferred it if you''d have left more of the detail in whichever channel contained the freckles, which would have preserved the contours of your model''s face.', '2005-05-11 04:49:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377349, 172868, 10261, '<td valign="top">I find the mosaic / cubist processing done on this image distracting. It seems to highlight the lines in the background, drawing attention away from the pencils. This might have looked better in B&amp;W, which would have highlighted the textures of your subject.</td>', 'I find the mosaic / cubist processing done on this image distracting. It seems to highlight the lines in the background, drawing attention away from the pencils. This might have looked better in B&W, which would have highlighted the textures of your subject.', '2005-05-11 04:53:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377350, 174446, 10261, '<td valign="top">I can''t tell if the dark shadow that Alan''s hiding in is supposed to be that of the cigarettes, or just a door. The lighting/shadows are a bit harsher than I''d like, but that''s typically one of the more difficult aspects of making forced perspective look real.</td>', 'I can''t tell if the dark shadow that Alan''s hiding in is supposed to be that of the cigarettes, or just a door. The lighting/shadows are a bit harsher than I''d like, but that''s typically one of the more difficult aspects of making forced perspective look real.', '2005-05-11 04:56:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377355, 174216, 10261, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done. I like the way that the leaves are illuminated. The only thing I''d rather not see is the moon, but that''s partially because it always looks fake when portrayed realistically in a photograph where it''s not the focal point (prima donna heavenly bodies). You did a nice job of placing just enough light around the man''s silhouette to clearly identify him as a person and not just an oddly shaped bit of foliage. If he were holding a torch rather than a flashlight it would give the image a very different feel, which I personally would find a bit more interesting.</td>', 'Very nicely done. I like the way that the leaves are illuminated. The only thing I''d rather not see is the moon, but that''s partially because it always looks fake when portrayed realistically in a photograph where it''s not the focal point (prima donna heavenly bodies). You did a nice job of placing just enough light around the man''s silhouette to clearly identify him as a person and not just an oddly shaped bit of foliage. If he were holding a torch rather than a flashlight it would give the image a very different feel, which I personally would find a bit more interesting.', '2005-05-11 05:05:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1377806, 173431, 27482, '<td valign="top">Not bad at all, I like this but I think this would have looked better in low key rather than high key but what the hell do I know.  Good shot, I gave it a pretty high score, hope you do well.</td>', 'Not bad at all, I like this but I think this would have looked better in low key rather than high key but what the hell do I know.  Good shot, I gave it a pretty high score, hope you do well.', '2005-05-11 10:29:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378227, 174216, 37659, '<td valign="top">Very interesting, stark contrast... feels like something out of the X-files.</td>', 'Very interesting, stark contrast... feels like something out of the X-files.', '2005-05-11 12:08:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378230, 173215, 37659, '<td valign="top">Beautifully soft, ethereal... great shot.</td>', 'Beautifully soft, ethereal... great shot.', '2005-05-11 12:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378252, 172293, 37659, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.</td>', 'Beautiful.', '2005-05-11 12:13:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378304, 174301, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is really excellent. I could imagine that just about anything could happen in this dreamscape. I love the corners. I''ve done some experimentation with that style myself and I really like it. Except of course my pictures look like crap compared to this lovely peice of work! I won''t be surprised to see this ribbon.<br/> <br/>I particularly like the starkness of the clouds in the center and the softness of the clouds as they approach the edges.</td>', 'This is really excellent. I could imagine that just about anything could happen in this dreamscape. I love the corners. I''ve done some experimentation with that style myself and I really like it. Except of course my pictures look like crap compared to this lovely peice of work! I won''t be surprised to see this ribbon. I particularly like the starkness of the clouds in the center and the softness of the clouds as they approach the edges.', '2005-05-11 12:23:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378321, 174486, 28710, '<td valign="top">Nice job. I like that the clouds also contain colour. If this was anything other than a perfect black silhouette, I would question it as a subject in the dreams topic.</td>', 'Nice job. I like that the clouds also contain colour. If this was anything other than a perfect black silhouette, I would question it as a subject in the dreams topic.', '2005-05-11 12:27:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378331, 173353, 28710, '<td valign="top">Super job of creating an illusion of movement. My eyes can hardly look at this without making me dizzy!</td>', 'Super job of creating an illusion of movement. My eyes can hardly look at this without making me dizzy!', '2005-05-11 12:30:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378383, 174505, 28710, '<td valign="top">Sweet location! I thought of a bunch of dumb things to say about what I would have liked to have seen in the model or the dandelion floaters and the blown out cherry blossoms, but then I remembered that this is yours and you have done an excellent job in composition, and  I think most people in my dreams wear pretty normal clothes like that too.<br/> <br/>The aligned branches are extraordinary!</td>', 'Sweet location! I thought of a bunch of dumb things to say about what I would have liked to have seen in the model or the dandelion floaters and the blown out cherry blossoms, but then I remembered that this is yours and you have done an excellent job in composition, and  I think most people in my dreams wear pretty normal clothes like that too. The aligned branches are extraordinary!', '2005-05-11 12:43:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378446, 174643, 28710, '<td valign="top">Shooting animals and babies can be really tough.  This is simply wild. Great choice with the negative. Those curtains just jump out at you and those flowers are superb as well. They look like calla lilies. Most cultures relate those to death. This pic is made even better with the light blues. I wouldn''t be surprised if the voters decided that this pic was worthy of a little more blue.</td>', 'Shooting animals and babies can be really tough.  This is simply wild. Great choice with the negative. Those curtains just jump out at you and those flowers are superb as well. They look like calla lilies. Most cultures relate those to death. This pic is made even better with the light blues. I wouldn''t be surprised if the voters decided that this pic was worthy of a little more blue.', '2005-05-11 12:56:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378655, 173379, 37630, '<td valign="top">Contrast of color on black and white makes this a riveting portrait</td>', 'Contrast of color on black and white makes this a riveting portrait', '2005-05-11 14:03:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1378975, 174583, 35161, '<td valign="top">The dreamy effect works well in this shot! :)</td>', 'The dreamy effect works well in this shot! :)', '2005-05-11 15:22:47.000000', NULL, 1),
