(1379552, 174691, 34852, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image, great effect! Ribbon worthy. Good luck!</td>', 'Beautiful image, great effect! Ribbon worthy. Good luck!', '2005-05-11 18:26:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379558, 174123, 34852, '<td valign="top">Excellent idea, very well done! Composition is great. 10</td>', 'Excellent idea, very well done! Composition is great. 10', '2005-05-11 18:29:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379576, 173059, 16488, '<td valign="top">Entirely sweet!  This is an exceptionally good example of a use for a super-wide angle lens.  The colors, the feel of the pic, the wonderful expression and pose of the dreamer--all work to convey the statement.  Well done!  Highest marks.</td>', 'Entirely sweet!  This is an exceptionally good example of a use for a super-wide angle lens.  The colors, the feel of the pic, the wonderful expression and pose of the dreamer--all work to convey the statement.  Well done!  Highest marks.', '2005-05-11 18:34:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379584, 172694, 34852, '<td valign="top">Amazing! Mysterious and dreamy image. Very well executed! 10</td>', 'Amazing! Mysterious and dreamy image. Very well executed! 10', '2005-05-11 18:36:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379586, 174020, 16488, '<td valign="top">Poignant and gritty!  The color binds this composition well.  Hard to look at, at first, but the execution of the image overcomes that.  Interesting statement.</td>', 'Poignant and gritty!  The color binds this composition well.  Hard to look at, at first, but the execution of the image overcomes that.  Interesting statement.', '2005-05-11 18:36:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379597, 174123, 16488, '<td valign="top">Imaginative and witty!  How well this fits the theme!  What is there to say?  Beautifully composed.  Interestingly stated.  Quirky. Playful.  I am soooo jealous of the talent you display--let it go to your head, if you will.  (A two-digit score for you.)</td>', 'Imaginative and witty!  How well this fits the theme!  What is there to say?  Beautifully composed.  Interestingly stated.  Quirky. Playful.  I am soooo jealous of the talent you display--let it go to your head, if you will.  (A two-digit score for you.)', '2005-05-11 18:40:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379601, 173431, 16488, '<td valign="top">I could look at this for almost ever....<br/> <br/>Lovely how the composition keeps the eye moving and resting, like a bride walking down the aisle of a church.</td>', 'I could look at this for almost ever.... Lovely how the composition keeps the eye moving and resting, like a bride walking down the aisle of a church.', '2005-05-11 18:41:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379660, 174216, 16488, '<td valign="top">Beautiful and well-titled!<br/> <br/>It reminds me of a poem by Stevie Smith:<br/> <br/>"Not Waving But Drowning"<br/> <br/>Nobody hear him, the dead man,<br/>But still he lay moaning:<br/>I was much further out than you thought<br/>And not waving but drowning.<br/> <br/>Poor chap, he alway loved larking<br/>And now he''s dead<br/>It must have been too cold for him his heart gave way,<br/>They said.<br/> <br/>Oh, no no no, it was too cold always<br/>(Still the dead one lay moaning)<br/>I was much too far out all my life<br/>And not waving but drowning.</td>', 'Beautiful and well-titled! It reminds me of a poem by Stevie Smith: "Not Waving But Drowning" Nobody hear him, the dead man,But still he lay moaning:I was much further out than you thoughtAnd not waving but drowning. Poor chap, he alway loved larkingAnd now he''s deadIt must have been too cold for him his heart gave way,They said. Oh, no no no, it was too cold always(Still the dead one lay moaning)I was much too far out all my lifeAnd not waving but drowning.', '2005-05-11 19:05:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379662, 174691, 16488, '<td valign="top">Cutely staged.  Props etc. make this look like a promo shot for a play.</td>', 'Cutely staged.  Props etc. make this look like a promo shot for a play.', '2005-05-11 19:06:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379666, 173619, 16488, '<td valign="top">Yes, that''s exactly what it feels like.  Simple concept so well done!</td>', 'Yes, that''s exactly what it feels like.  Simple concept so well done!', '2005-05-11 19:07:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379708, 174696, 25257, '<td valign="top">crop it more</td>', 'crop it more', '2005-05-11 19:26:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379711, 172694, 25257, '<td valign="top">better focus!</td>', 'better focus!', '2005-05-11 19:28:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379717, 173619, 25257, '<td valign="top">your focussing could be better!!</td>', 'your focussing could be better!!', '2005-05-11 19:33:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1379763, 174400, 25257, '<td valign="top">hurts eyes!</td>', 'hurts eyes!', '2005-05-11 19:52:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380080, 173250, 10261, '<td valign="top">I feel like the person, building, and balcony in the bottom right corner were included as an excuse for the photoshopped clouds which dominate the rest of the image. The strong line at the top of the building enhances the appearance that these are two separate compositions, both of which have a clear, but only mildly interesting focal point. I think that the composition would be improved if there was a greater attempt to tie the two segments of the image together (e.g. having the figure on the balcony looking expectantly toward the converging cloud formation, and possibly burning the clouds at the center of the spiral to make the focal point enigmatic rather than anti-climactic).<br/> <br/>On a purely technical note, there isn''t enough light on the front of the figure on the balcony to clearly make out any features. This may have been a creative decision to refrain from anchoring the figure''s identity to a particular person, but it feels more like you neglected to bounce enough light onto the person''s front side. A fill flash or a reflector could have helped with this. The pronounced difference in contrast between the bottom corner and the cloud formation seems like an overdone attempt to direct the viewer''s attention.<br/> <br/>This is a very creative vision, but I feel that with some straightforward changes it could easily be a ribbon winner.</td>', 'I feel like the person, building, and balcony in the bottom right corner were included as an excuse for the photoshopped clouds which dominate the rest of the image. The strong line at the top of the building enhances the appearance that these are two separate compositions, both of which have a clear, but only mildly interesting focal point. I think that the composition would be improved if there was a greater attempt to tie the two segments of the image together (e.g. having the figure on the balcony looking expectantly toward the converging cloud formation, and possibly burning the clouds at the center of the spiral to make the focal point enigmatic rather than anti-climactic). On a purely technical note, there isn''t enough light on the front of the figure on the balcony to clearly make out any features. This may have been a creative decision to refrain from anchoring the figure''s identity to a particular person, but it feels more like you neglected to bounce enough light onto the person''s front side. A fill flash or a reflector could have helped with this. The pronounced difference in contrast between the bottom corner and the cloud formation seems like an overdone attempt to direct the viewer''s attention. This is a very creative vision, but I feel that with some straightforward changes it could easily be a ribbon winner.', '2005-05-11 23:19:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380106, 174693, 10261, '<td valign="top">Since this is the "Dreams" challenge, the person sleeping seems kind of unnecessary. The props suggest what the content of your dreams may be, but I think that even in isolation any of them might have been used to create a much stronger, more visceral feeling for what law enforcement entails than the caricature that the unembellished accessories give me. Letting your audience''s imaginations fill in the juicy details is a good thing, but expecting them to also write the screenplay for you is expecting a bit too much.<br/></td>', 'Since this is the "Dreams" challenge, the person sleeping seems kind of unnecessary. The props suggest what the content of your dreams may be, but I think that even in isolation any of them might have been used to create a much stronger, more visceral feeling for what law enforcement entails than the caricature that the unembellished accessories give me. Letting your audience''s imaginations fill in the juicy details is a good thing, but expecting them to also write the screenplay for you is expecting a bit too much.', '2005-05-11 23:29:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380136, 174081, 10261, '<td valign="top">The ambiguous title complements the equally ambiguous photograph. The light suggests that this was taken outdoors within a few hours of midday. The shadows would have been much better if it were overcast or earlier / later, but if this was some kind of a performance by a third-party, then you may have had no alternatives. The shadowy figures in the background are particularly intriguing, but the rather high-key figures in the foreground eclipse them. Both figures are obviously doing something quite intentionally, but since I''m not given any clear indication of what''s going on I''m left with a prevailing sense of confusion rather than having the image elicit any strong emotion. Although this is a more literal representation of the bizarre character of most dreams, my waking mind would be more at ease with your image if the composition offered me some clear fixation point (e.g. the thing in the guy''s hand) on which I might base my interpretation of this picture.</td>', 'The ambiguous title complements the equally ambiguous photograph. The light suggests that this was taken outdoors within a few hours of midday. The shadows would have been much better if it were overcast or earlier / later, but if this was some kind of a performance by a third-party, then you may have had no alternatives. The shadowy figures in the background are particularly intriguing, but the rather high-key figures in the foreground eclipse them. Both figures are obviously doing something quite intentionally, but since I''m not given any clear indication of what''s going on I''m left with a prevailing sense of confusion rather than having the image elicit any strong emotion. Although this is a more literal representation of the bizarre character of most dreams, my waking mind would be more at ease with your image if the composition offered me some clear fixation point (e.g. the thing in the guy''s hand) on which I might base my interpretation of this picture.', '2005-05-11 23:43:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380148, 173276, 10261, '<td valign="top">Although the muted colors of the background lend this picture a restful feeling, I think that the silhouette would have been stronger against the more war-like backdrop which you''d get by dramatically increasing the saturation and setting the sky on fire.</td>', 'Although the muted colors of the background lend this picture a restful feeling, I think that the silhouette would have been stronger against the more war-like backdrop which you''d get by dramatically increasing the saturation and setting the sky on fire.', '2005-05-11 23:50:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380156, 173500, 10261, '<td valign="top">The hand and sleeve seem to be the recipient of the duck''s wrath, but it looks like it was pasted in from another image as an afterthought. The high saturation of the grass and the ducks implies that they are the intended subjects, but the drab, flat looking (glowing) hand which lies at the focal point seems anticlimactic.</td>', 'The hand and sleeve seem to be the recipient of the duck''s wrath, but it looks like it was pasted in from another image as an afterthought. The high saturation of the grass and the ducks implies that they are the intended subjects, but the drab, flat looking (glowing) hand which lies at the focal point seems anticlimactic.', '2005-05-11 23:56:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380160, 174021, 10261, '<td valign="top">Although this picture is rich with mood, it would be well on it''s way to nightmarish if there was a more well-defined victim whose terror-stricken face was clearly visible.<br/></td>', 'Although this picture is rich with mood, it would be well on it''s way to nightmarish if there was a more well-defined victim whose terror-stricken face was clearly visible.', '2005-05-11 23:59:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380170, 172613, 10261, '<td valign="top">I really like the DOF and the well-defined arc formed by the cluster of flowers. The rather fuzzy, over-sharpened look of the petals drops my enjoyment of this image down a few notches though.</td>', 'I really like the DOF and the well-defined arc formed by the cluster of flowers. The rather fuzzy, over-sharpened look of the petals drops my enjoyment of this image down a few notches though.', '2005-05-12 00:02:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380181, 173344, 10261, '<td valign="top">One day what? "One day my mottled balls will win a blue ribbon"? The frosted border seems a bit too pronounced, and (yes, I''m nit-picking) you appear to be unable to decide whether you''d like to win a pair of blue streamers or a gold medal. Personally, I''d recommend shooting for the one that can be traded for "L" glass.<br/></td>', 'One day what? "One day my mottled balls will win a blue ribbon"? The frosted border seems a bit too pronounced, and (yes, I''m nit-picking) you appear to be unable to decide whether you''d like to win a pair of blue streamers or a gold medal. Personally, I''d recommend shooting for the one that can be traded for "L" glass.', '2005-05-12 00:11:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380188, 173011, 23098, '<td valign="top">Good perspective -- Sanibel is a dream place for me.</td>', 'Good perspective -- Sanibel is a dream place for me.', '2005-05-12 00:17:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380190, 173886, 23098, '<td valign="top">Most definetly!</td>', 'Most definetly!', '2005-05-12 00:17:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380197, 174687, 23098, '<td valign="top">Wow! Good one!</td>', 'Wow! Good one!', '2005-05-12 00:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380227, 174290, 10261, '<td valign="top">This is a really interesting effect. I can make out two (possibly 3, if that''s one in the bottom right) faces, which appear to belong to the same woman, but can''t determine anything other than that. As a semi-abstract image, this is good. The title implies that you may have intended a somewhat deeper meaning; if this is the case, an exposure which was a little clearer in presenting recognizable features may have helped to better convey your intent.</td>', 'This is a really interesting effect. I can make out two (possibly 3, if that''s one in the bottom right) faces, which appear to belong to the same woman, but can''t determine anything other than that. As a semi-abstract image, this is good. The title implies that you may have intended a somewhat deeper meaning; if this is the case, an exposure which was a little clearer in presenting recognizable features may have helped to better convey your intent.', '2005-05-12 00:41:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380234, 174547, 10261, '<td valign="top">I like the clean lines in this picture as well as the strong visual momentum flowing from the upper right corner to the lower left. I''m a little unclear on how this relates to the challenge, though.</td>', 'I like the clean lines in this picture as well as the strong visual momentum flowing from the upper right corner to the lower left. I''m a little unclear on how this relates to the challenge, though.', '2005-05-12 00:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380235, 174270, 10261, '<td valign="top">This is a decent photograph of a lion, but the title reinforces the idea that this has little to do with the challenge topic.</td>', 'This is a decent photograph of a lion, but the title reinforces the idea that this has little to do with the challenge topic.', '2005-05-12 00:45:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380242, 174400, 23098, '<td valign="top">Soaring through the air. Nice effect.!</td>', 'Soaring through the air. Nice effect.!', '2005-05-12 00:48:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380245, 173393, 10261, '<td valign="top">I see two large, parallel rocks with ocean waves flowing between them. Without referring to the metaphor in the title, I''d have interpreted this an another "I wish I was on the beach" type picture. If your intent was to depict the metaphor, I think that I should see a boat or something being dashed against one of the rocks.</td>', 'I see two large, parallel rocks with ocean waves flowing between them. Without referring to the metaphor in the title, I''d have interpreted this an another "I wish I was on the beach" type picture. If your intent was to depict the metaphor, I think that I should see a boat or something being dashed against one of the rocks.', '2005-05-12 00:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380246, 174695, 23098, '<td valign="top">Cute and clever.</td>', 'Cute and clever.', '2005-05-12 00:50:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380250, 172472, 10261, '<td valign="top">I understand the title, but what is the person in the picture doing? Threshing the sand?</td>', 'I understand the title, but what is the person in the picture doing? Threshing the sand?', '2005-05-12 00:52:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380254, 172456, 10261, '<td valign="top">The fact that the hand is held palm up makes this look more like this was posed against a spotted wall and less like the person is swimming for the surface (which would almost certainly involve the palms facing down).</td>', 'The fact that the hand is held palm up makes this look more like this was posed against a spotted wall and less like the person is swimming for the surface (which would almost certainly involve the palms facing down).', '2005-05-12 00:55:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380267, 172096, 10261, '<td valign="top">This looks like the type of snapshot one gets if one drops their camera on the ground and the shutter happens to fire. Without any particularly interesting cloud formation or a clear focal point, this just looks like a random section of clouds. The B&amp;W emphasizes the texture of the clouds, but I think that in this case the (presumably) blue sky would have been more interesting than the shades of gray.</td>', 'This looks like the type of snapshot one gets if one drops their camera on the ground and the shutter happens to fire. Without any particularly interesting cloud formation or a clear focal point, this just looks like a random section of clouds. The B&W emphasizes the texture of the clouds, but I think that in this case the (presumably) blue sky would have been more interesting than the shades of gray.', '2005-05-12 01:01:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380270, 174446, 12253, '<td valign="top">Returning for comment: Very funny.  I am pretty sure I know how you did this (cigarette pack in front of monitor or printed picture), but we''ll see.   It''s perfect for dream.  I like how you concealed the brand name here and the use of dramatic lighting.  Bumping up!</td>', 'Returning for comment: Very funny.  I am pretty sure I know how you did this (cigarette pack in front of monitor or printed picture), but we''ll see.   It''s perfect for dream.  I like how you concealed the brand name here and the use of dramatic lighting.  Bumping up!', '2005-05-12 01:02:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380278, 173353, 12253, '<td valign="top">Return for comment: Wow, that''s excellent control of the camera movement blur with some stop action--or is this a filter?  I can''t tell, but if it''s motion blur, you perfected it!   I am curious how you did this.  Good luck in the challenge.  Top marks from me.<br/> <br/>Edit: Removed wrong guess about model!  Nice work.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-13 00:31:22.</i></td>', 'Return for comment: Wow, that''s excellent control of the camera movement blur with some stop action--or is this a filter?  I can''t tell, but if it''s motion blur, you perfected it!   I am curious how you did this.  Good luck in the challenge.  Top marks from me. Edit: Removed wrong guess about model!  Nice work.', '2005-05-12 01:05:31.000000', '2005-05-13 01:31:22.000000', 1),
(1380282, 174505, 10261, '<td valign="top">This image has a pinkish cast, which I find distracting. The DOF seems to restrict the focus to the first few feet of the image, leaving the rest of the image an odd, not-quite-in-focus feeling. If the focus were softer overall or the DOF were either much shallower or encompassed the entire image I''d have liked the presentation better. I think that rendering this in B&amp;W would have emphasized the depth of the image, as the color seems to exist mainly in the periphery.</td>', 'This image has a pinkish cast, which I find distracting. The DOF seems to restrict the focus to the first few feet of the image, leaving the rest of the image an odd, not-quite-in-focus feeling. If the focus were softer overall or the DOF were either much shallower or encompassed the entire image I''d have liked the presentation better. I think that rendering this in B&W would have emphasized the depth of the image, as the color seems to exist mainly in the periphery.', '2005-05-12 01:06:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380288, 174364, 12253, '<td valign="top">Returning for comment.  Excellent surreal shot perfect for dreams.  It works well here, but I wonder if you also tried desaturating the face but not the lips?  I''d be curious to see that version if it works as well or better than this one (which is great!)</td>', 'Returning for comment.  Excellent surreal shot perfect for dreams.  It works well here, but I wonder if you also tried desaturating the face but not the lips?  I''d be curious to see that version if it works as well or better than this one (which is great!)', '2005-05-12 01:07:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1380292, 173059, 12253, '<td valign="top">Returning for comment.  Great concept, very well done.  My pick for a ribbon!   Top marks from me.</td>', 'Returning for comment.  Great concept, very well done.  My pick for a ribbon!   Top marks from me.', '2005-05-12 01:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
